{
  "editions": [
    {
      "edition": "standard",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ὁ οὖν Κύριος ἰδὼν τὴν ἁπλότητα αὐτῶν καὶ πᾶσαν νηπιότητα",
          "english_quote": "When the Lord saw their sincerity and their complete childlike innocence,",
          "issue": "The inferential connective οὖν is omitted. “When” conveys the circumstance of seeing but not the connection between the believers’ preceding conduct and the Lord’s response.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “Therefore, when the Lord saw their sincerity and their complete childlike innocence, …” Review the revised sentence against the source before adoption.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ ἐνδεδυμένοι ⸢τὸ⸣ πνεῦμα ⸢τὸ ἅγιον⸣ τούτων τῶν παρθένων",
          "english_quote": "The house/clothing and virgins imagery is retained;",
          "issue": "The note claims that house imagery is retained, but neither the selected clause nor this section’s English contains house imagery. Clothing and virgins are present; the added house reference misdescribes this translation.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace this portion with “The clothing and virgins imagery is retained.” If a contextual house reference is intended, identify its separate location and distinguish it from imagery translated in this section.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "simplified",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ πάντοτε σπλάγχνον ἔχοντες ἐπὶ πάντα ἄνθρωπον",
          "english_quote": "They had compassion for everyone.",
          "issue": "The simplified edition omits πάντοτε, “always,” from the compassion clause. The preceding sentence’s “always” modifies rejoicing, not this separately stated characteristic.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “They always had compassion for everyone.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ὁ οὖν Κύριος ἰδὼν τὴν ἁπλότητα αὐτῶν καὶ πᾶσαν νηπιότητα",
          "english_quote": "The Lord saw their sincerity and complete childlike innocence.",
          "issue": "The inferential οὖν is omitted, removing the explicit connection with the preceding description of their conduct.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider beginning the sentence “Therefore, the Lord saw …,” or retaining the relationship in a joined sentence: “Therefore, when the Lord saw …, he …” Review the complete replacement before adoption.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐπλήθυνεν αὐτοὺς ἐν τοῖς κόποις τῶν χειρῶν αὐτῶν",
          "english_quote": "He made their work prosper",
          "issue": "The simplification drops “of their hands,” an explicit source image describing their labor. “Their work” preserves the general activity but not the complete wording pattern.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “He made them prosper in the work of their hands.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐδοκίμασε γὰρ ὑμᾶς ὁ Κύριος καὶ ἐνέγραψεν ὑμᾶς εἰς τὸν ἀριθμὸν τὸν ἡμέτερον",
          "english_quote": "The Lord tested you and enrolled you in our number.",
          "issue": "The explanatory γὰρ is omitted. The source explicitly presents the Lord’s testing and enrollment as grounds for the preceding assurance; the simplified sentence merely follows it.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “For the Lord tested you and enrolled you in our number.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ ἐνδεδυμένοι ⸢τὸ⸣ πνεῦμα ⸢τὸ ἅγιον⸣ τούτων τῶν παρθένων",
          "english_quote": "The house/clothing and virgins imagery is retained;",
          "issue": "The note claims retention of house imagery that is absent from both this selected section and its simplified translation.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace this portion with “The clothing and virgins imagery is retained.” Any contextual house reference needs a separate locator and an explicit distinction from this section’s translated imagery.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "λέγω δὲ ὑμῖν τοῖς τοιούτοις οὖσιν ἐγὼ ὁ ἄγγελος τῆς μετανοίας· διαμείνατε τοιοῦτοι",
          "english_quote": "Preserve repentance conditions, confession, mercy and healing, and the declared foolishness, childlikeness/gentleness and spirit/seed alternatives.",
          "issue": "The section-specific simplification metadata includes confession, mercy, healing, and a foolishness alternative, none of which occurs in this selected section. The supplied report locates the foolishness case in S.9.xxii.4, not S.9.xxiv. This conflates decisions for different units.",
          "suggested_revision": "Limit this record to decisions actually applicable here: remaining as described, the offspring promises, and the disclosed childlikeness/gentleness and spirit/seed alternatives. Move other decisions to their corresponding units.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions substantially follow the selected working Greek, preserve the speaker, negations and offspring promises, and use policy-compatible servant and repentance terminology. Revision is needed for omitted source elements and inaccurate notes or metadata. The conjecture and variant disclosures agree with the supplied bounded project report; neither working reading needs replacement merely because an alternative exists. This review does not authenticate unseen manuscripts or certify exhaustive collation. All proposed replacements require fresh review."
}
